DP  - 2023 Dec 17
TI  - [The role of potassium-competitive acid blockers in the treatment of acid-related 
      digestive diseases].
PG  - 1967-1973
LID - 10.1556/650.2023.32937 [doi]
AB  - Potassium-competitive acid blockers inhibit the H+/K+ exchange in gastric mucosal 
      parietal cells and thus decrease the HCl secretion more efficiently. These drugs 
      were synthesized in Eastern-Asian countries, and three were marketed. Vonoprazan 
      and tegoprazan are superior to proton-pump inhibitors in the initial and 
      maintenance treatment of erosive gastroesophageal reflux disease. These drugs are 
      equivalent to lansoprazol in curing peptic ulcers. Vonoprazan and 
      tegoprazan-based triple therapies were superior to proton-pump based regimens in 
      eradicating Helicobacter pylori, but the North-American–European randomised study 
      confirmed these results in part only. Cost-effectiveness studies confirmed the 
      superiority of the new class of drugs over proton-pump inhibitors. Further 
      randomised studies performed in other countries/continents would appear necessary 
      to determine the role of potassium-competitive acid blockers in the treatment of 
      acid-related diseases. Orv Hetil. 2023; 164(50): 1967–1973.
